/* book Worked example: Q: An MSMPR crystallizer for ammonium sulfate (ρ = 1770 kg/m³, kv = 1) has τ = 2.0 h. A sample gives population densities n = 1.84 × 109, 6.77 × 108, 2.49 × 108 and 9.16 × 107 per (m³ mm) at L = 0.2, 0.4, 0.6 and 0.8 mm. Find G, n°, B°, NT, MT and LD.
   1. ln n = 21.33, 20.33, 19.33 and 18.33. Each 0.2 mm step lowers ln n by 1.00, so the slope is −5.00 per mm.
   2. Gτ = 1/5.00 = 0.200 mm; G = 0.200/2.0 = 0.100 mm/h.
   3. Intercept: ln n° = 21.33 + 5.00 × 0.2 = 22.33, so n° = 5.0 × 109 per (m³ mm).
   4. B° = n°G = 5.0 × 109 × 0.100 = 5.0 × 108 nuclei per m³ per h. NT = n°Gτ = 5.0 × 109 × 0.200 = 1.0 × 109 crystals per m³.
   5. In metres: n° = 5.0 × 1012 per (m³ m) and Gτ = 2.0 × 10−4 m. MT = 6 × 1 × 1770 × 5.0 × 1012 × (2.0 × 10−4)4 = 6 × 1770 × 5.0 × 1012 × 1.6 × 10−15 = 85.0 kg/m³.
   6. LD = 3Gτ = 0.60 mm; number mean 0.20 mm; mass-weighted mean 0.80 mm.
   Answer: G = 0.10 mm/h, n° = 5.0 × 109 per (m³ mm), B° = 5.0 × 108 per (m³ h), NT = 1.0 × 109 per m³, MT = 85 kg/m³, LD = 0.60 mm. */
