/* book Worked example 2: Q: An ED stack with 100 cell pairs desalts 1.0 m³/h of water from 2000 to 500 mg/L NaCl at a current efficiency of 0.90 and a stack voltage of 120 V. Find the current, the power and the energy per m³ of product.
   1. ΔC = (2000 − 500)/58.44 = 25.67 mol/m³. Q = 1.0/3600 = 2.778 × 10−4 m³/s, so salt removed = 7.13 × 10−3 mol/s.
   2. I = zFQΔC/(εN) = 1 × 96 485 × 7.13 × 10−3/(0.90 × 100) = 688/90 = 7.64 A.
   3. Power = VI = 120 × 7.64 = 917 W.
   4. Energy per m³ = 0.917 kW × 1 h/1.0 m³ = 0.92 kWh/m³, for the stack alone (pumping is extra).
   Answer: I = 7.6 A, power 0.92 kW, energy 0.92 kWh per m³ of product. */
