/* book exam traps: The RO driving force is ΔP − Δπ, not ΔP alone; at 15 bar the net here is only 11 bar. | π = iCRT needs C in mol/m³ and i = 2 for NaCl; using mg/L or forgetting i gives nonsense. | Rejection uses concentrations, recovery uses flows; a 95 % rejection membrane can run at 50 % or 75 % recovery. | In ultrafiltration beyond the gel point, raising the pressure does not raise the flux; stirring or cross-flow does. | The same current passes through all N cell pairs in series, so it removes N times the salt one cell pair would; leaving N out of I = zFQΔC/(εN) overstates the current N-fold. */
